{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/961462-where-are-the-rules-for-lifting-stuff","id":961462,"title":"Where are the Rules for Lifting Stuff ?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-31T22:47:14-07:00","id":961462,"title":"Where are the Rules for Lifting Stuff ?","content":"I wanted to know where are the rules for lifting heavy Objects ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T23:51:21-07:00","id":961481,"title":"","content":"For whatever reason they seem to have been largely skipped in the 2e books, but the 1e lifting/feats of strength charts should still work fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T14:12:51-07:00","id":962963,"title":"","content":"Ah thanks. So how much could you lift for 30 strength ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T14:45:49-07:00","id":962973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/961462-where-are-the-rules-for-lifting-stuff?p=962963#post962963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah thanks. So how much could you lift for 30 strength ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Extrapolating from that chart? 21,000 lbs","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T15:00:08-07:00","id":962979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/961462-where-are-the-rules-for-lifting-stuff?p=962963#post962963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah thanks. So how much could you lift for 30 strength ?</div> </div> </div> </div>WHERE can you have numbers like that?! Ephemeral Beings cannot have more like Power 20, Horrors go up to Strenght 10.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T16:00:06-07:00","id":962990,"title":"","content":"Vampire with a few merits and then going full beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T16:17:39-07:00","id":962994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/961462-where-are-the-rules-for-lifting-stuff?p=962990#post962990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampire with a few merits and then going full beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>And people say mages are overpowered...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T16:52:07-07:00","id":963001,"title":"","content":"Page 94 of the CofD core book, &quot;Improvised Weapons&quot;, states you can use an object as an improvised weapon, its Size being the Strength requirement to use it.<br /> Page 90 of the same book, &quot;Range&quot;, states you can only throw objects if the object's size is below your Strength.<br /> <br /> By these rules a Compact Car can be used effectively as an improvised weapon (including throwing it at your opponents) with a character that has 9 Strength.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11641,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","user":"Yelesom","date":". 09-03-2016, 08:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T20:53:10-07:00","id":963079,"title":"","content":"Vampires with the riding the wave style get double their BP as bonus dice on strength rolls, so a BP 10 vamp with 10 strength would have a base lifting power of 10 + 35-40 dice (I assume anyone with 10 strength isn't going to have less than 5 stamina). The actual lifting capacity varies with the roll, but it's safe to say you'll rarely see less than 10 successes, for a total effective lifting value of 20 or more.<br /> <br /> Honestly at that point just assume you can chuck anything the size of a 18 wheeler or less, although lifting it in one piece might not work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T20:59:32-07:00","id":963080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/961462-where-are-the-rules-for-lifting-stuff?p=963079#post963079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires with the riding the wave style get double their BP as bonus dice on strength rolls, so a BP 10 vamp with 10 strength would have a base lifting power of 10 + 35-40 dice (I assume anyone with 10 strength isn't going to have less than 5 stamina). The actual lifting capacity varies with the roll, but it's safe to say you'll rarely see less than 10 successes, for a total effective lifting value of 20 or more.<br /> <br /> Honestly at that point just assume you can chuck anything the size of a 18 wheeler or less, although lifting it in one piece might not work.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's before factoring in Vigor and Physical Intensity.<br /> <br /> (Yeah, BP 10 vampires are ridiculous, but then again so is every template at Power Stat 10.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}